1
00:01:00,479 --> 00:01:01,280
You're awake

2
00:01:01,439 --> 00:01:03,479
Your brothers sent all these things

3
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,319
I brought them up for you

4
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,920
This one's from Awen

5
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:09,159
No message with it

6
00:01:09,359 --> 00:01:11,120
This one's from Xie Guanhong

7
00:01:11,599 --> 00:01:13,519
He wishes you a speedy recovery

8
00:01:23,079 --> 00:01:24,319
Now don't get too worked up

9
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,560
Getting too worked up isn't good for you

10
00:02:30,319 --> 00:02:32,520
This is all the big boss gets to eat?

11
00:02:35,319 --> 00:02:36,960
Times are tough, you know.

12
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,680
The economy's going downhill.

13
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,400
You're lucky to have anything to eat.

14
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:42,759
Have you eaten?

15
00:02:43,319 --> 00:02:44,120
I'm not eating.

16
00:02:45,199 --> 00:02:46,400
This is just for the prisoners.

17
00:03:04,439 --> 00:03:05,520
I saw it.

18
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,840
So you noticed.

19
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,879
You deserve a Best Actor award.

20
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,280
Fine.

21
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,479
But you're pretty impressive.

22
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,400
Sitting in a police station,

23
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,080
and you got Cannon to kill himself.

24
00:03:20,039 --> 00:03:20,840
Amazing.

25
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:21,840
What?

26
00:03:22,919 --> 00:03:24,199
Cannon killed himself.

27
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,439
Oh my God.

28
00:03:29,439 --> 00:03:31,280
I talked with Cannon for a while.

29
00:03:31,919 --> 00:03:33,039
He couldn't speak,

30
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,240
but he could write.

31
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:38,560
He wrote a few things down for me.

32
00:03:49,319 --> 00:03:51,879
Can Cannon even read?

33
00:03:57,199 --> 00:03:58,400
He told me everything.

34
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:02,199
How you showed up at the scene,

35
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,560
how you got into a fight with his men,

36
00:04:04,879 --> 00:04:06,439
how you burned down his house.

37
00:04:07,639 --> 00:04:08,879
Every single detail.

38
00:04:09,199 --> 00:04:10,199
He didn't write down everything,

39
00:04:11,159 --> 00:04:12,360
but it's pretty interesting.

40
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,480
If I follow this lead,

41
00:04:17,879 --> 00:04:20,560
I should dig up something, huh?

42
00:04:26,079 --> 00:04:27,319
You're really in no rush at all.

43
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,759
Why the hurry?

44
00:04:31,519 --> 00:04:32,839
Let me tell you something.

45
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:36,759
I've been fighting with my wife lately.

46
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:39,120
You know she's got quite a temper.

47
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:40,639
So, you see,

48
00:04:40,879 --> 00:04:43,279
you'll just be in here for 48 hours.

49
00:04:43,639 --> 00:04:44,800
Get some good rest.

50
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:46,879
It's good you're not in a rush.

51
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,759
But your company sure is in a panic.

52
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,560
Your company's books have always been off.

53
00:04:55,959 --> 00:04:57,120
Can't be helped.

54
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,399
Laundering money too fast

55
00:04:58,399 --> 00:05:00,199
easily leads to problems.

56
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,759
Independent Commission Against Corruption

57
00:05:15,839 --> 00:05:18,079
has probably frozen your accounts by now.

58
00:05:25,639 --> 00:05:26,800
Independent Commission Against Corruption

59
00:05:36,959 --> 00:05:39,040
Why can't I get through, brother?

60
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:48,279
I run a company.

61
00:05:48,279 --> 00:05:49,480
Legit and by the book.

62
00:05:49,759 --> 00:05:50,800
Who did I offend now?

63
00:05:51,439 --> 00:05:52,800
A legit company, huh.

64
00:05:53,439 --> 00:05:54,720
But my records show

65
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,360
that under your company's name,

66
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,639
money's shuffled between a dozen accounts.

67
00:05:59,519 --> 00:06:01,240
Plus some funds coming in from overseas.

68
00:06:02,319 --> 00:06:04,120
You've also got a charity fund.

69
00:06:04,879 --> 00:06:06,319
Lots of donations.

70
00:06:06,959 --> 00:06:09,040
But the numbers are all a mess.

71
00:06:09,639 --> 00:06:10,680
This kind of thing,

72
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,319
isn't it called Money laundering?

73
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:16,920
Isn't Money laundering handled by

74
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,720
the Commercial Crime Bureau?

75
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:20,560
Officer Chen, you're with the anti-triad squad.

76
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,399
Brother Jiadong,

77
00:06:25,959 --> 00:06:27,319
a grown man like you,

78
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,720
haven't you got a mind of your own?

79
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,600
Ah Hong,

80
00:06:30,959 --> 00:06:32,160
do you remember what I told you?

81
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,560
Break the law, and you're the first I'll nab.

82
00:06:36,319 --> 00:06:37,920
Nab me?

83
00:06:38,879 --> 00:06:40,360
I'm squeaky clean.

84
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:41,519
What would you nab me for?

85
00:06:42,199 --> 00:06:43,000
Well, that doesn't matter.

86
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,680
So just sit tight in here for a while.

87
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:46,959
I'm not afraid to tell you,

88
00:06:47,279 --> 00:06:48,560
that case with Camel,

89
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,759
we've got a new lead.

90
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,920
Besides your fingerprints at the scene,

91
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,519
we found one more person's prints too.

92
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,279
That suspect,

93
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:57,879
he's in the next room.

94
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,240
Want to know who he is?

95
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,480
It's your son.

96
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,439
Xie Zihao.

97
00:07:08,959 --> 00:07:10,519
I really don't know anything.

98
00:07:11,079 --> 00:07:12,639
Just let me out of here.

99
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:14,600
I don't know a thing!

100
00:07:16,439 --> 00:07:17,600
I didn't see anything.

101
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,639
Don't ask me.

102
00:07:18,639 --> 00:07:20,439
I don't know anything.

103
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:25,920
Coming after me, fine.

104
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:26,879
But you go after my son?

105
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:29,680
That's just bad manners.

106
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:30,759
What I'm doing,

107
00:07:31,639 --> 00:07:32,439
it's called Procedure.

108
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,879
Go after my son,

109
00:07:37,079 --> 00:07:38,720
and I'll wipe out your whole family.

110
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:41,360
That's a bit extreme, isn't it?

111
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:43,879
If I don't bring him back in,

112
00:07:44,519 --> 00:07:46,399
how do I face the victim?

113
00:07:52,079 --> 00:07:54,519
Remember to fix my AC when you get time.

114
00:08:21,399 --> 00:08:23,240
The wind outside's picking up.

115
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:24,800
And when it blows,

116
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:27,319
my knees start aching.

117
00:08:27,759 --> 00:08:30,279
Uncle Fat, cut to the chase.

118
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,240
You came to see me.

119
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,200
What is it you want to say?

120
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:36,759
Still a man of few words, just like before.

121
00:08:36,879 --> 00:08:39,759
But you always see things clearly.

122
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:43,360
Your friend was too ruthless,

123
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:45,320
and yet he left a mess behind.

124
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,720
Camel's the current boss of the Dongxing Gang.

125
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,399
He killed Camel.

126
00:08:51,399 --> 00:08:52,559
Do you have any idea

127
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,960
just how big a mess he's made?

128
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:57,200
I don't know about all those politics.

129
00:08:57,399 --> 00:08:58,440
All I know is,

130
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:02,279
making Camel the prize was your idea.

131
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,399
I tried to warn him.

132
00:09:05,399 --> 00:09:06,200
He wouldn't listen.

133
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,759
And now you come to warn me.

134
00:09:07,799 --> 00:09:09,039
I told you long ago,

135
00:09:09,039 --> 00:09:10,919
I don't meddle in Heyisheng's affairs.

136
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:12,279
You don't need to say all this.

137
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:15,639
This thing isn't so simple.

138
00:09:45,159 --> 00:09:45,960
I don't know.

139
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,279
I don't know.

140
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,799
I don't know.

141
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,440
I don't know.

142
00:10:01,519 --> 00:10:03,200
I don't know.

143
00:10:03,559 --> 00:10:04,879
Camel is dead.

144
00:10:04,879 --> 00:10:06,840
Now the whole city's in an uproar.

145
00:10:08,039 --> 00:10:10,639
Dongxing's crew will definitely retaliate.

146
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:12,480
When you live in this world,

147
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,600
isn't retaliation pretty normal?

148
00:10:15,039 --> 00:10:18,440
Besides, he's the one who killed Cannon.

149
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:21,759
I know you don't believe me.

150
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,600
So let me be blunt.

151
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,600
Ah Hong, you know,

152
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:29,600
he's got no loyalty and breaks all the rules.

153
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:32,279
He doesn't deserve to be our Dragon Head.

154
00:10:32,559 --> 00:10:34,360
The Major Crimes Unit took Xie Guanhong.

155
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:35,320
Can't reach him.

156
00:10:36,639 --> 00:10:37,480
The Economic Crime Unit

157
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:39,240
has been digging for hours now.

158
00:10:40,039 --> 00:10:41,679
If they dig up anything crucial,

159
00:10:41,799 --> 00:10:43,440
all of Heyisheng will collapse.

160
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:49,039
I told you all long ago,

161
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:50,759
do it cleanly.

162
00:10:51,879 --> 00:10:54,360
Chen Jiadong isn't so easy to deal with.

163
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:56,200
He's like a rabid dog.

164
00:10:57,120 --> 00:11:00,679
Once he bites down, he won't let go.

165
00:11:25,159 --> 00:11:27,679
I've already met with a few of the Elders.

166
00:11:28,159 --> 00:11:29,519
At a time like this,

167
00:11:29,799 --> 00:11:32,000
someone has to step up

168
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,320
and hold things together.

169
00:11:33,519 --> 00:11:36,240
You're the best man for the job.

170
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:41,600
You're loyal, and you can fight.

171
00:11:42,519 --> 00:11:44,919
You've done so much for the gang.

172
00:11:46,039 --> 00:11:47,080
The brothers,

173
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,720
they really respect you.

174
00:11:57,399 --> 00:11:59,840
Who are you trying to buy off with this?

175
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,240
This is just a show of good faith.

176
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:10,120
If those two get out safe,

177
00:12:10,279 --> 00:12:12,799
you'll get every last cent you're owed.

178
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Save your breath.

179
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,519
I got out a long time ago.

180
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:19,000
Dragon Head, the gang, whatever,

181
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,039
None of it is my business anymore.

182
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:23,799
I just want to be a law-abiding citizen

183
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:25,480
and live my own life in peace.

184
00:12:27,399 --> 00:12:28,639
Ah Qiang,

185
00:12:28,759 --> 00:12:30,799
you can step away, sure.

186
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:32,200
But

187
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:35,600
will you just watch your brother die?

188
00:12:35,679 --> 00:12:36,600
What do you mean?

189
00:12:37,759 --> 00:12:40,200
Well, aren't you the clever dealmaker.

190
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,440
But you know as well as I do,

191
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,360
I'm about to retire.

192
00:12:44,159 --> 00:12:48,000
All this money means nothing to me now.

193
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:49,919
You think you can just walk away clean?

194
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:54,279
All these years,

195
00:12:54,399 --> 00:12:56,600
How many kickbacks from Heyisheng?

196
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:57,919
How much dirty money did you pocket?

197
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,799
Every single one of those deals,

198
00:12:59,799 --> 00:13:02,039
It's all on Xie Guanhong's USB drive.

199
00:13:02,639 --> 00:13:03,879
If they find out,

200
00:13:04,279 --> 00:13:05,559
we all go down.

201
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:10,360
You're threatening me.

202
00:13:11,639 --> 00:13:13,240
I'm just reminding you,

203
00:13:13,799 --> 00:13:15,480
we're all in the same boat.

204
00:13:17,399 --> 00:13:18,519
If you won't step up,

205
00:13:19,039 --> 00:13:20,679
then we do it by the rules.

206
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:23,360
He killed his own brother.

207
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:26,200
It's not just a simple expulsion.

208
00:13:27,919 --> 00:13:29,440
If you're the one who does it,

209
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:31,200
it's better than us doing it.

210
00:13:32,039 --> 00:13:33,519
You're his brother.

211
00:13:33,519 --> 00:13:35,080
You'll know when to hold back.

212
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,279
Whether to spare his life or not,

213
00:13:37,759 --> 00:13:40,279
that's your call to make.

214
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:46,600
I know you're the most loyal of us all.

215
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:49,840
But loyalty isn't just to one person.

216
00:13:50,039 --> 00:13:51,440
It's to everyone.

217
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:53,399
It's to the whole gang.

218
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:57,360
Only you can save our face,

219
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,720
keep the rules,

220
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:03,039
and still spare his life.

221
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:04,840
Uncle Fat,

222
00:14:05,159 --> 00:14:06,320
why do we

223
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:08,600
have to take the same old road?

224
00:14:08,879 --> 00:14:09,919
What's wrong with settling down

225
00:14:09,919 --> 00:14:11,840
and running an honest business?

226
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:15,279
I'm old now.

227
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:18,960
There's so much I want to do but can't.

228
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,759
All I want now

229
00:14:21,919 --> 00:14:25,080
is to protect the turf I fought for.

230
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:28,240
Everything else, I can't handle anymore.

231
00:14:28,919 --> 00:14:30,559
You'll be the Dragon Head.

232
00:14:31,519 --> 00:14:32,679
Heyisheng,

233
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:34,919
where it goes from here,

234
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:37,559
that's still your call.
